{%- comment -%}
  fye-page-type — the single source of truth for "what kind of page is this".

  WHY THIS EXISTS: on the xCloud app-proxy filter pages (/a/search...) both
  `request.page_type` and `template.name` come back EMPTY, so body classes and
  template gates silently fail. The old theme worked around this in three
  separate places with three slightly different fallbacks.

  Outputs a single lowercase token. Capture it once in layout/theme.liquid and
  pass it down; never re-derive it.

    {%- capture fye_page_type -%}{%- render 'fye-page-type' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign path = request.path | downcase
  assign type = request.page_type

  # App-proxy pages report nothing. Resolve from the path instead.
  if path contains '/a/search'
    assign type = 'search'
  elsif path contains '/a/wishlist'
    assign type = 'wishlist'
  elsif path contains '/a/compare'
    assign type = 'compare'
  elsif type == blank
    assign type = template.name
  endif

  if type == blank
    assign type = 'page'
  endif

  echo type | strip
-%}
